{# One batch of comments plus the sentinel that pulls the next, as
   post_feed_fragment.jinja is for drawings. `comments` is built by
   comments_context() in handlers/home.rs: `rows`, and `next_url` while a
   full batch says there may be more. A profile's (handlers/profile.rs)
   also says `by_drawing`: every row there is by the same person, so each
   is headed by the drawing it is on instead (comment_card_macro.jinja). Rendered inline for the first batch
   -- beside a feed (comments_aside_macro.jinja), on a feed's comments page
   (home_comments.jinja), a community's, a tag's, a profile's tab --
   and standalone by the load-more handlers for the rest, so it must not
   depend on anything those handlers do not pass.

   Beside a feed the list scrolls on its own, and the sentinel is revealed
   when that list is scrolled to it: htmx watches with an
   IntersectionObserver, which counts the list's own clipping. #}
{% import "comment_card_macro.jinja" as comment_card_macro %}
{% for comment in comments.rows %}
  {{ comment_card_macro.comment_card(comment, r2_public_endpoint_url, ftl_get_message, by_drawing=comments.by_drawing) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if comments.next_url %}
  <div class="infinite-scroll-sentinel"
       hx-get="{{ comments.next_url }}"
       hx-trigger="revealed"
       hx-swap="outerHTML">
    <span class="loading-indicator">{{ ftl_get_message("loading-more-comments") }}</span>
  </div>
{% endif %}
